oto/msid-133261447,imgsize-770719.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[7.7 magnitude earthquake hits Indonesia: 38 killed, buildings collapse; 5 visuals of devastation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133260331.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A significant earthquake registering 7.7 on the Richter scale rocked eastern Indonesia early Saturday, claiming the lives of at least thirty-eight individuals and leading to the destruction of various structures. Ongoing rescue missions are striving to aid the affected population, while landslides and widespread power failures hinder relief efforts in some areas. Although a tsunami alert was briefly raised, it was later cancelled after confirming that sea conditions were stable.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/7-7-magnitude-earthquake-hits-indonesia-38-killed-buildings-collapse-5-visuals-of-devastation/articleshow/133260331.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/7-7-magnitude-earthquake-hits-indonesia-38-killed-buildings-collapse-5-visuals-of-devastation/articleshow/133260331.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T16:26:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133260948,imgsize-13892988.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK searches for homes with air conditioning jump 104% as heatwaves intensify]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133260877.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Searches for homes with air conditioning in the UK have more than doubled this summer. Repeated heatwaves prompt buyers to pay greater attention to property cooling capabilities. Many households are making practical changes to keep cool during hotter weather. Britain's housing stock faces concerns about coping with increasingly hotter summers. This shift influences buyer priorities and what they are willing to purchase.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/uk-searches-for-homes-with-air-conditioning-jump-104-as-heatwaves-intensify/articleshow/133260877.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/uk-searches-for-homes-with-air-conditioning-jump-104-as-heatwaves-intensify/articleshow/133260877.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T16:28:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI News Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133261022,imgsize-140696.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK PM Andy Burnham announces £65m support package for farmers hit by drought]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133260516.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-andy-burnham-announces-65m-support-package-for-farmers-hit-by-drought/articleshow/133260516.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-andy-burnham-announces-65m-support-package-for-farmers-hit-by-drought/articleshow/133260516.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T16:04:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133260580,imgsize-868900.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ukraine strikes Russian aerospace facility and MiG-31 base in overnight attacks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133260276.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-strikes-russian-aerospace-facility-and-mig-31-base-in-overnight-attacks/articleshow/133260276.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-strikes-russian-aerospace-facility-and-mig-31-base-in-overnight-attacks/articleshow/133260276.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T15:53:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133260454,imgsize-172278.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1958, 58 pigs were removed from Clipperton, helping seabirds grow to 137,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133259630.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Feral pigs introduced to Clipperton Island devastated seabird populations and land crabs. Ornithologist Kenneth Stager removed fifty-eight pigs, allowing the ecosystem to gradually recover. This removal helped the seabird colony grow from 650 to over 137,000 birds. Later, black rats arrived, impacting the island's vegetation and bird populations negatively. Clipperton's story highlights invasive species' profound ecological effects on islands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1958-58-feral-pigs-were-removed-from-clipperton-island-helping-a-seabird-colony-grow-from-650-to-more-than-137000/articleshow/133259630.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1958-58-feral-pigs-were-removed-from-clipperton-island-helping-a-seabird-colony-grow-from-650-to-more-than-137000/articleshow/133259630.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T14:51:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133259676,imgsize-1769103.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jellyfish became a threat to France's Gravelines plant after clogging cooling systems]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133259246.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a striking environmental incident, a massive jellyfish swarm has compelled the shutdown of reactors at France's Gravelines nuclear plant. The clogged seawater cooling systems have brought significant disruption to power generation. Following a related incident in 2025, the plant introduced enhanced monitoring and fishing strategies. This occurrence underscores the vulnerabilities faced by coastal nuclear installations amidst the challenges posed by extreme summer temperatures affecting France's nuclear output.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/jellyfish-turned-into-an-unexpected-threat-to-frances-gravelines-nuclear-plant-after-a-huge-swarm-clogged-its-cooling-system/articleshow/133259246.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/jellyfish-turned-into-an-unexpected-threat-to-frances-gravelines-nuclear-plant-after-a-huge-swarm-clogged-its-cooling-system/articleshow/133259246.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T16:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133259365,imgsize-680132.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The ground beneath Poland's wind turbines became nesting grounds for wild bees]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133259052.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Poland, the bases of wind turbines have emerged as surprising havens for pollinators. Research highlights that these zones foster a thriving community of wild bees and a variety of plant species. The bare gravel and low maintenance create perfect nesting sites for ground-nesting bees. While butterflies opt for grasslands, both flies and grasslands flourish equally in these overlooked yet vital habitats for biodiversity on farmland.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/the-ground-beneath-394-foot-wind-turbines-in-poland-became-unexpected-nesting-and-feeding-grounds-for-wild-bees-in-farmland/articleshow/133259052.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/the-ground-beneath-394-foot-wind-turbines-in-poland-became-unexpected-nesting-and-feeding-grounds-for-wild-bees-in-farmland/articleshow/133259052.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133259142,imgsize-1355597.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The Lac La Belle sank in a Lake Michigan storm, but its wreck stayed hidden]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133258455.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1872-the-lac-la-belle-sank-in-a-lake-michigan-storm-but-its-wreck-stayed-hidden-until-a-60-year-search-finally-paid-off/articleshow/133258455.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1872-the-lac-la-belle-sank-in-a-lake-michigan-storm-but-its-wreck-stayed-hidden-until-a-60-year-search-finally-paid-off/articleshow/133258455.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T14:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133258691,imgsize-201098.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The Sahara once held a lake 48% larger than all five Great Lakes combined]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133258726.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/the-sahara-once-held-a-lake-48-larger-than-all-five-great-lakes-combined-but-mega-chad-vanished-about-5000-years-ago/articleshow/133258726.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/the-sahara-once-held-a-lake-48-larger-than-all-five-great-lakes-combined-but-mega-chad-vanished-about-5000-years-ago/articleshow/133258726.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133258824,imgsize-236618.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China's new solar plant made with 15,927 mirrors will power 50,000 homes while saving 60,000 tons of coal annually]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133258203.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[China has proudly completed the construction of the world's tallest solar thermal power plant at an impressive altitude of over 15,000 feet. Known as the Tushuo facility, this 100 MW powerhouse utilizes mirrors to effectively concentrate solar energy onto molten salts. The resulting stored heat will generate electricity even after sunset, ultimately supplying power to approximately 50,000 households each year once connected to the grid.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/china-completes-installation-of-15927-mirrors-concentrating-heat-at-1040-f-at-worlds-highest-solar-thermal-plant-will-power-50000-homes-while-saving-60000-tons-of-coal-annually/articleshow/133258203.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/china-completes-installation-of-15927-mirrors-concentrating-heat-at-1040-f-at-worlds-highest-solar-thermal-plant-will-power-50000-homes-while-saving-60000-tons-of-coal-annually/articleshow/133258203.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T12:54:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133258216,imgsize-1367916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[24-year-old archaeology enthusiast helps uncover a 3,700-year-old stone circle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133258725.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/24-year-old-archaeology-enthusiast-helps-uncover-a-3700-year-old-stone-circle-hidden-in-an-english-forest/articleshow/133258725.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/24-year-old-archaeology-enthusiast-helps-uncover-a-3700-year-old-stone-circle-hidden-in-an-english-forest/articleshow/133258725.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133258869,imgsize-308598.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas reactor reached criticality in a year, aiming to produce medical isotopes ]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133258459.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-small-texas-reactor-reached-criticality-in-under-a-year-aiming-to-produce-medical-isotopes-that-us-hospitals-now-import/articleshow/133258459.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-small-texas-reactor-reached-criticality-in-under-a-year-aiming-to-produce-medical-isotopes-that-us-hospitals-now-import/articleshow/133258459.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133258570,imgsize-137546.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Connecticut cemetery leased unused land for 7,000 solar panels]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133258460.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-connecticut-cemetery-leased-unused-land-for-7000-solar-panels-but-the-ground-beneath-them-could-become-habitat-for-bees-and-pollinators/articleshow/133258460.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-connecticut-cemetery-leased-unused-land-for-7000-solar-panels-but-the-ground-beneath-them-could-become-habitat-for-bees-and-pollinators/articleshow/133258460.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T13:19:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133258502,imgsize-290054.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Vera Wang: Teen scientist finds fungi that can break down plastic, sunscreen]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133257660.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-vera-wang-the-hawaii-high-school-senior-who-built-a-coconut-based-ocean-filter-as-a-sophomore-two-years-later-she-found-fungi-in-coconut-husks-that-can-biodegrade-plastic-and-sunscreen/articleshow/133257660.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-vera-wang-the-hawaii-high-school-senior-who-built-a-coconut-based-ocean-filter-as-a-sophomore-two-years-later-she-found-fungi-in-coconut-husks-that-can-biodegrade-plastic-and-sunscreen/articleshow/133257660.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T13:02:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133257714,imgsize-1071094.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota teen builds system that cut seizure recurrence by 70.1% in worms]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133257848.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Evan Morris created a low-cost system using worms and ultrasound.  This system helps study seizure suppression and reduces recurrence by seventy percent.  The project utilizes sonogenetics and a computer-controlled closed-loop detection method.  Morris received a significant award for his innovative life science research.  His work offers a faster, less expensive platform for neuroscience exploration.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/minnesota-teen-evan-morris-built-a-low-cost-system-that-detected-seizure-like-activity-in-worms-and-triggered-ultrasound-recurrence-fell-70-1-in-his-model/articleshow/133257848.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/minnesota-teen-evan-morris-built-a-low-cost-system-that-detected-seizure-like-activity-in-worms-and-triggered-ultrasound-recurrence-fell-70-1-in-his-model/articleshow/133257848.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133257873,imgsize-119052.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Archaeologists find young woman buried with fetus in a Swedish cave; remains may be up to 9,500 years old]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133256944.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable archaeological find, researchers uncovered the ancient remains of a pregnant woman along with her fetus in a Swedish cave. Dating back approximately 8,000 to 9,500 years, this discovery ranks among the earliest known burials of pregnant women. Future investigations will involve DNA analysis and radiocarbon dating to gain further insights. The cave is likely to have been used for the burial of other individuals as well.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeologists-found-a-young-woman-believed-to-be-14-to-19-buried-with-a-32-to-34-week-fetus-in-a-swedish-cave-the-remains-may-be-up-to-9500-years-old/articleshow/133256944.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeologists-found-a-young-woman-believed-to-be-14-to-19-buried-with-a-32-to-34-week-fetus-in-a-swedish-cave-the-remains-may-be-up-to-9500-years-old/articleshow/133256944.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T11:36:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133257134,imgsize-2386634.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Begin discussions': South Korea's Lee Jae Myung calls for talks with North Korea]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133255725.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[South Korean President Lee Jae Myung seeks peace talks to formally end the Korean War.  He also wants to discuss North Korea's nuclear capabilities and reduce regional tensions.  This proposal comes as North Korea strengthens its military ties with Russia.  Annual US-South Korean military exercises are scheduled to begin soon.  Lee also addressed improving relations with Japan and fostering prosperity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/begin-discussions-south-koreas-lee-jae-myung-calls-for-talks-with-north-korea/articleshow/133255725.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/begin-discussions-south-koreas-lee-jae-myung-calls-for-talks-with-north-korea/articleshow/133255725.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T10:03:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI News Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133255858,imgsize-682679.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump claims ‘young, beautiful girls’ thank him for making Washington safer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133254526.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-claims-young-beautiful-girls-thank-him-for-making-washington-safer/articleshow/133254526.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-claims-young-beautiful-girls-thank-him-for-making-washington-safer/articleshow/133254526.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-15T08:24:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133254605,imgsize-93020.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Until cause is known: US Army temporarily halts Apache training missions after Texas crash]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133253820.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-army-temporarily-halts-apache-